tegrated reporting, and separately permits annual-fee payment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u9.2011"},{"reason":"Operational review and enquiry arrangements; no exception to mandatory submission.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035"},{"reason":"Issuing division identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u11.2191"},{"reason":"Issuing institution identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u12.2220"},{"reason":"Document end marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u13.2256"},{"reason":"Identifies investment-product categories associated with IPD administration.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not independently determine route compliance.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control concerns submission events to IPD for investment products it administers. The text does not restrict the obligation to a named class of banks, licensees or individual users. Reporting requests are included; annual-fee settlement is described separately.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"The footnote lists relevant product categories; the background identifies new applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions. WINGS is expanded, but detailed boundaries of a submission event and IPD administration are not supplied.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270","d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain accepted during the extended parallel run. No post-cutover exemption, outage dispensation or grandfathering provision is stated. Optional annual-fee payment is a separate capability, rather than an exception to mandatory submission.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' establishes the submission-route requirement. 'Will be integrated' describes system integration; 'can also settle' permits annual-fee payment without requiring that payment route.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The extended parallel run ends on 29 November 2024 and mandatory use begins on 30 November 2024. The original 29 October end date is superseded. Treatment of follow-up acts on existing cases is not expressly detailed.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 circular is referenced but not supplied. Dependency missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a has no supplied text or hash; its identity and effect cannot be established. Neither omission supplies evidence of an exception.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the referenced 8 July 2024 circular or the missing dependency specify treatment of follow-up submissions for cases opened before the cutover?","What event fixes the submission date where transmission, receipt and acceptance fall on different dates?","Does any supplied-later authoritative material define exclusions or outage arrangements? None is stated in this packet."],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The selected control evaluates one application or submission event, not the compliance of an institution as a whole.","A submission event is classified using its substance and IPD administration; the fact supplier must resolve uncertain classifications.","The event date is supplied as a Gregorian date. The packet does not resolve transmission-versus-receipt timing.","Extension of the parallel run preserves the described acceptance of existing channels through 29 November 2024.","No grandfathering rule is inferred merely because a case began before the cutover."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"quote":"new product applications and post-authorisation/registration submissions to IPD.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"quote":"the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"}],"distinction":"The strongest supported reading attaches the cutover to each submission event. For example, an IPD-administered fund's NAV report submitted on 30 November 2024 through the old system fails this selected route control, even if the fund was authorised earlier. A fee-only payment outside e-IP does not fail this control merely because of its route. The packet supports neither a general grandfathering alternative nor mandatory e-IP payment of annual fees; treating either as a competing rule would invent ambiguity. The strongest uncertainty concerns follow-up acts in pending cases and the event fixing their submission date.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, including applicable post-authorisation/registration reporting. Fee-only settlement does not itself establish this classification.","name":"is_covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date of the assessed submission event; resolving which event fixes this date may require interpretation where transmission and receipt differ.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"Whether the assessed application or submission was submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["For an existing case, which follow-up communications qualify as distinct applications or submissions subject to the cutover?","Do the unavailable referenced materials supply transition mechanics that affect event classification or timing?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected mandatory e-IP submission-route control, when scope is true, the result answers whether this submission used e-IP: true means the route requirement is met; false means it is not met. Outside scope, this control makes no compliance determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.","subject":"Mandatory e-IP route for an individual IPD investment-product application or submission from 30 November 2024"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Establishes the extended parallel period and mandatory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"reason":"Background heading; supplies no independent condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u1.427"},{"reason":"Identifies the launch date, WINGS portal, earlier circular and new-product and post-authorisation/registration functions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439"},{"reason":"Describes the original parallel period and acceptance of existing channels; informs the meaning of the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"reason":"Section heading; supplies no independent condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u4.956"},{"reason":"Reports monitoring and engagement; does not condition mandatory routing.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u5.1013"},{"reason":"Confirms the revised end date; enhancements explain the extension without expressly conditioning cutover.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"reason":"Heading supports the transition context but adds no independent rule.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u7.1505"},{"reason":"Restates mandatory routing, identifies reports to be integrated and permits annual-fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading; supplies no independent condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u9.2011"},{"reason":"Operational review and contact guidance do not expressly create routing exceptions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u11.2191"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u12.2220"},{"reason":"End marker; supplies no substantive condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u13.2256"},{"reason":"Lists product categories associated with IPD scope; whether the list is exhaustive remains unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not independently define successful submission through e-IP.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The route requirement attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD. It is transaction-specific, without an express restriction to banks or named classes of submitter. Whether the footnote exhaustively limits product scope is unresolved.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is identified as the investment-product application/submission system on WINGS; WINGS is expanded in footnote 2. Applications and submissions are illustrated by new-product work, post-authorisation/registration work and specified reporting. The packet does not define when a submission is completed or accepted.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u17.2522"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels are accepted during the parallel period, whose extension naturally carries that acceptance through 29 November 2024. No post-cutover exception for outages, pending cases or unfinished enhancements is stated. 'Where practicable' qualifies operational review and enhancement, not the mandatory submission route.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528","d19f9ecf9fd26.u10.2035"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' imposes the routing requirement. 'Will be integrated' describes system migration; 'can also settle' permits fee settlement through e-IP without expressly requiring that payment route. The selected control tests only submission routing.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The revised parallel period ends on 29 November 2024 and mandatory routing begins on 30 November 2024 inclusively. The earlier 29 October endpoint is superseded. The packet does not expressly resolve pending-case grandfathering or the controlling timestamp for a submission.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737","d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The earlier circular dated 8 July 2024 is referenced but not supplied. Dependency missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a has no supplied text or source hash, so its content and relationship to that circular cannot be established. The packet supports the cutover rule but cannot resolve operational details or qualifications in omitted material.","source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively delimit the covered investment products, or describe the products ordinarily administered by IPD?","Does the cutover apply to every submission event on or after 30 November 2024, including further material in cases opened through existing channels?","Which timestamp and completion criteria determine whether an item was submitted via e-IP?","What does dependency missing.4ad6b317ad4ade41b82f120a contain, and does the earlier 8 July 2024 circular supply relevant definitions or transitional qualifications?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The unit of evaluation is one application or submission event, not an institution's overall compliance.","The applicable date is the date of that event; the source does not establish the operational timestamp used to assign it.","The cutover applies to submission events in both new and existing cases; no express grandfathering is supplied.","Whether the relevant investment product is administered by IPD remains an externally supplied classification. The footnote informs that classification without an assumed exhaustive-list rule.","Extending the parallel run preserves the described acceptance of existing channels through its revised end date.","No omitted dependency is assumed to contain an exception, and no omitted exception is assumed absent as a matter of law."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u6.1187"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"}],"distinction":"This proposed event-based reading makes the route mandatory for covered submission events from the cutover, including later submissions in existing cases. A case-opening interpretation could grandfather earlier cases, but the supplied text contains no express support sufficient to formalize that alternative. Similarly, mandatory submission routing does not make the separately permitted annual-fee payment route mandatory. The strongest uncertainty is whether omitted transitional material changes treatment of pending cases.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product; a standalone fee payment is not included merely because e-IP can process it.","name":"is_product_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the evaluated event"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned by the evaluated event is administered by IPD, with footnote 1 informing the classification.","name":"product_administered_by_ipd","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the relevant product"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date assigned to the evaluated application or submission event under the applicable submission-timing criteria; those criteria are not specified in the packet.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The evaluated application or submission was submitted to IPD through e-IP; determining completed submission may require operational criteria absent from this packet.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean routing outcome for the evaluated event"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_product_application_or_submission product_administered_by_ipd (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Do omitted transition provisions grandfather any existing cases or particular reporting requests?","Are fee-related documents independently applications or submissions even where payment itself is optional through e-IP?","What evidence establishes a completed e-IP submission rather than a draft, upload attempt or rejected transmission?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] Selected control: mandatory e-IP routing for a covered submission event. Within the declared scope—an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product dated on or after 30 November 2024—true means the event satisfies this routing requirement because it was submitted via e-IP; false means it fails this routing requirement. Outside that scope, this control gives no compliance verdict. Unknown inputs remain unknown. This is a proposed interpretation of routing alone.","subject":"Mandatory e-IP route after the extended parallel run"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the extended parallel run and mandatory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u1.427"},{"reason":"Identifies launch, portal, submission categories and an earlier circular whose contents are unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the original parallel run.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"reason":"Heading introducing the extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u4.956"},{"reason":"Explains monitoring and consultation; supplies no selected routing condition.","st