l run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"}],"distinction":"This proposed event-based reading makes the route mandatory for covered submission events from the cutover, including later submissions in existing cases. A case-opening interpretation could grandfather earlier cases, but the supplied text contains no express support sufficient to formalize that alternative. Similarly, mandatory submission routing does not make the separately permitted annual-fee payment route mandatory. The strongest uncertainty is whether omitted transitional material changes treatment of pending cases.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product; a standalone fee payment is not included merely because e-IP can process it.","name":"is_product_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u2.439","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the evaluated event"},{"meaning":"The investment product concerned by the evaluated event is administered by IPD, with footnote 1 informing the classification.","name":"product_administered_by_ipd","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u16.2270"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the relevant product"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date assigned to the evaluated application or submission event under the applicable submission-timing criteria; those criteria are not specified in the packet.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The evaluated application or submission was submitted to IPD through e-IP; determining completed submission may require operational criteria absent from this packet.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d19f9ecf9fd26.u0.0","d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean routing outcome for the evaluated event"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_product_application_or_submission product_administered_by_ipd (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Do omitted transition provisions grandfather any existing cases or particular reporting requests?","Are fee-related documents independently applications or submissions even where payment itself is optional through e-IP?","What evidence establishes a completed e-IP submission rather than a draft, upload attempt or rejected transmission?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] Selected control: mandatory e-IP routing for a covered submission event. Within the declared scope—an application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product dated on or after 30 November 2024—true means the event satisfies this routing requirement because it was submitted via e-IP; false means it fails this routing requirement. Outside that scope, this control gives no compliance verdict. Unknown inputs remain unknown. This is a proposed interpretation of routing alone.","subject":